Chapter: BvtRockStart
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeGameRules
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeGatherer
  cites Uoaix chapter BritainProduction
  cites Uoaix chapter EconomyGatherer
  cites Uoaix chapter EconomyHarvest
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

 Trial 46700: Britain's gatherer, its ore node spent, searched the same four rock faces every step from game hour 71
 (blocked 64 to 352), its search starting at its trips alone. A miner with no failure starts where it did (trips, kind);
 each failed search (blocked) starts the next one cgg-rock-plans faces on (L-FUTILITY). Answers 7 when all three hold.
  brst-checks : Integer -> Integer
  brst-checks (unused) = when bb-economy 0
    is Err (_) -> -1
    is Ok (x) -> let r = cgg-resource-of x.world 31 0
      in when egg-new-for x 3703 cgg-place r 0
        is Err (_) -> -2
        is Ok (g) -> let spot = BbSpot { x = 1473, y = 1517, z = 20 }
          in let c = cgg-make-in cgg-britain g 0 spot spot 0 0 0 174
          in let fresh = cgg-rock-start c
          in let a = __record-set c "blocked" 1
          in let once = cgg-rock-start c
          in let b = __record-set c "blocked" 3
          in let thrice = cgg-rock-start c
          in (if fresh == 174 + cgg-kind c - cgg-place then 1 else 0) + (if once == fresh + cgg-rock-plans then 2 else 0) + (if thrice == fresh + 3 * cgg-rock-plans then 4 else 0)
  bvt-rock-start : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-rock-start (unused) = act
    n <- brst-checks 0
    bvt-check ("a spent miner's failed rock search starts the next one past the faces it tried, and one that never failed starts as before (trial 46700, L-FUTILITY; code " & show n & ")") (n == 7)
  end
